{
  "requirement": "requirements.ci.errors",
  "file": "src/evidence.rs",
  "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
  "queries": [
    "early_exits",
    "error_accumulators"
  ],
  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]` declares `let mut errors = Vec::new();`, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`.\n\n**Violation match.** The only early exit flagged is `fs::canonicalize(root)?`. It runs before `errors` exists and before any check has run. Every later check takes `root` and depends on it, so a repository root that cannot be resolved leaves nothing meaningful to validate. The `?` therefore does not skip a later check that is independent of a failed one. It is harmless here.\n\n**Continuing after failures.** Each check records its failure in `errors` and the function carries on:\n- `crate::config::load_workspace_evidence` pushes its error and does not return.\n- `book_source_dir` falls back to `md` after a malformed `book.toml`. This matches the requirement that a malformed file is one failed check and that independent checks still run.\n- `collect_definitions` continues after an invalid name, an unclosed fence, or an unreadable chapter.\n- The remaining checks are all called unconditionally, each with `&mut errors`: `validate_setup`, the evidence-file loop, the missing-evidence loop, `collect_references_with_progress`, `validate_committed_credentials`, `sites::discover`, `validate_references`, `citations::validate`, `sites::validate`, and the two `rust_coverage` validators.\n- The `errors` loop over evidence files has no early exits. A file with no matching definition gets its \"no matching requirement or example\" error and still goes through `validate_evidence_file`.\n\n**Duplicate reports.** `discovery_errors` is a separate list. It is seeded from `errors` and extended with `errors[scanned..]`, so it does not add copies to `errors`. `validate_setup` reads `.config/nextest.toml` and `Cargo.toml` through `workspace_root`. It does not re-parse `habeas.toml`, so it does not repeat the `load_workspace_evidence` error. I found no place where one failure is reported twice.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
      "hash": "788e24af357372441e74b0823319d6b50ee4c071637fc9a47eb30d05e94d654d"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
